#!/bin/sh
# Let the guard PRINT. Redirecting it to /dev/null makes a failure look
# exactly like a pass, because a failing run prints nothing of its own.
set -e
node tools/syntax-guard.mjs .
node tools/version-guard.mjs
node tools/fade-guard.mjs .

node tools/listing-guard.mjs

# The notes converter and the notes/watchlist file split. Both run in plain
# Node, and the file guard evaluates app.js's own functions rather than a
# copy of them.
node tools/notes-guard.mjs
node tools/notes-file-guard.mjs

# A selection per tab, out of one set. Eleven readers share it, and any one
# of them forgetting to scope acts on rows nobody can see.
node tools/selection-guard.mjs

# Every link in an imported file has to reach a list. A video id is swept out
# of the whole text, so it survives any line shape while a page address did
# not. Both halves are asserted: the shapes arrive, and prose stays prose.
node tools/import-guard.mjs

# Fifty rows drawn, and every record still counted. The page is not a filter,
# so every count and both bulk actions read the whole filtered set.
node tools/pager-guard.mjs

# A swipe changes tabs and must do nothing else. Two clicks competed for it:
# the rating, and the row that opens its link.
node tools/swipe-guard.mjs

# A shared link reaches the Bookmarks tab or the YouTube tab, never Notes.
# The add writes a note on that tab, which is right for the button and wrong
# for a share: the reader did not choose the tab the share arrived on.
node tools/share-guard.mjs

# Asking to link, on a first run. Four things have to be true, and each one
# is a reason not to ask. A card that appears where any of them is false is
# nagging, and nagging is the one failure a first-run prompt has.
node tools/ask-guard.mjs

# The message under the paste field says which kind it is. Three tones, and
# each one is a shape as well as a colour: colour alone would leave a reader
# who cannot separate red from orange with one mark and three meanings.
node tools/status-guard.mjs

# The runtime sits beside the count, so it is short. Three units from the
# largest that is not zero, which answers the no-seconds-in-days rule.
node tools/runtime-guard.mjs

# A hover sticks to the last thing a finger tapped, so every hover rule sits
# behind a device that has a pointer. Tapping a tab and swiping away left its
# fill painted on a tab nobody was on.
node tools/hover-guard.mjs

# One menu, two kinds of item. Three write a file out of the lists and one
# fetches the Android installer, and a release carries both the .apk and the
# .aab that cannot be installed on a phone.
node tools/export-guard.mjs

# The share patch runs only in CI, where nothing watches it. Its clauses are
# proven here instead, so a clause that stops firing fails a commit.
node tools/android-share-fix.mjs --self-test
node tools/android-updater.mjs --self-test
